// Interrupt state — the declared contexts.
//
// `ints_off` is the SR save/mask/restore bracket (`move.w sr,-(sp)` /
// `move.w #$2700,sr` … `move.w (sp)+,sr`) as an ACQUIRED context: the compiler
// splices both halves and PROVES every path through the body reaches the
// restore. A caller that exposes SR in its contract declares the claim its
// WHOLE BODY earns, not the one the bracket alone would: `preserves(sr.mask)`
// when any instruction outside the bracket writes flags on a path to return —
// the release restores the caller's mask, but post-bracket flag traffic makes
// the CCR half false (and a bracket whose save is mid-proc restores mid-proc
// flags, never the caller's) — and bare `preserves(sr)` only when every CCR
// effect sits inside the pair. Either spelling's mask half is enforced by the
// spliced save/restore, which satisfies the balance check on its own. The
// adopter owns the WHY comment at the bracket: atomicity rationales are site
// facts, not context facts. Every consumer in the tree declares one of these
// spellings, so the clause reads as the contract and never as a lint's
// pressure: `[proc.sr-undeclared]` does NOT charge a consumer for the SR traffic
// this context splices in, because that traffic is declared HERE.
//
// `ints_off_until_rte` is `ints_off` FOR AN INTERRUPT HANDLER, and it is the same
// mask with a cheaper end. The 68000 pushes SR before it vectors, and `rte` pops
// it back — so a handler that raises the mask for its body has its restore
// performed by the return instruction it was going to execute anyway. The
// ordinary bracket's `move.w sr,-(sp)` (14 cyc) and `move.w (sp)+,sr` (16 cyc) in
// that position are 30 cycles spent producing a value the very next instruction
// discards: the pop writes IPL 4 (the level the CPU entered at), and `rte`
// immediately overwrites it with the pre-interrupt SR from the frame. Dropping
// them also CLOSES a window rather than opening one — between the pop and the
// `rte` the ordinary shape sits one instruction at IPL 4, where a level-6 VBlank
// can still nest into a handler that has finished tidying up.
//
// It is a flavour and not a second hand-spelling because the compiler can prove
// the thing that makes it safe. `released_by_rte` names the release instead of
// splicing it, and sigil then requires that EVERY path out of the bracket is, or
// falls straight onto, an `rte` (`[context.rte-undischarged]`); an acquire that
// pushes is refused outright (`[context.rte-acquire-pushes]`), because `rte`
// takes its exception frame off the stack top and a push with no matching pop
// would return through it. A bare `move.w #$2700, sr` in a handler body earns
// none of that: it is `User`-authored, so `[proc.sr-undeclared]` charges it, and
// neither honest clause can absorb it — `clobbers(sr)` is false of an
// interrupt-transparent handler, and `preserves(sr)` cannot be verified because
// the checker has no model of `rte` restoring it (declaring it collapses the
// whole preserves clause, so every movem-saved register then reports undeclared).
// That gap is the entire reason this context exists.
//
// ADOPTERS ARE IRQ HANDLERS ONLY. A proc reached by `jbsr` returns with `rts`,
// which does not touch SR, and the flavour will say so at the bracket rather than
// let the mask leak into the caller.
//
// `vblank` is a GRANTED context: the VBlank window cannot be acquired, only
// entered by the hardware. `grants(vblank)` on an interrupt entry point is a
// TRUST ROOT — the assembler cannot verify hardware dispatch, so the assertion
// is greppable and auditable rather than proven. What IS proven is the other
// side: a proc declaring `requires(vblank)` may only be called from inside the
// window (`[context.unsatisfied]`), so a VBlank-only routine can no longer be
// reached from the main loop by accident.
//
// Sites that stay HAND-SPELLED by design (a bracket is one lexical region with
// one entry and one exit): multi-exit brackets (one save, several
// restore-and-return paths — the DMA-queue transfer core); loops that re-mask
// under a single save (Sound_Init's alive-wait); and long spans whose masked
// region is a whole code block with its own internal structure
// (Section_RedrawPlanes, BG_Init, Sound_DrainSfxRing). STRUCTURAL exclusion: any
// bracket with a CCR out-contract can NEVER adopt — the full-SR restore
// overwrites CCR, so those sites pin their carry AFTER the restore (the
// DMA-queue core's andi/ori-to-ccr ordering). A hand-spelled site whose CCR does
// not round-trip declares the SR HALVES instead of the bare token:
// `preserves(sr.mask)` beside its flag result (the DMA-queue core) or beside
// `clobbers(sr.ccr)` (Sound_DrainSfxRing's empty fast path) — the partition
// check reads the split from the signature.
//
// Consumers `use engine.irq.{ints_off}` / `use engine.irq.{ints_off_until_rte}` /
// `use engine.irq.{vblank}`.
//
// Pure comptime module: opens no section and emits ZERO bytes anywhere in the
// ROM — bytes appear only where a consumer brackets with it.
module engine.irq

pub context ints_off {
    acquire = asm {
        move.w  sr, -(sp)
        move.w  #$2700, sr
    }
    release = asm {
        move.w  (sp)+, sr
    }
}

pub context ints_off_until_rte {
    acquire = asm {
        move.w  #$2700, sr
    }
    released_by_rte
}

pub context vblank { granted }
